    description:
      "Olympic Maximum is the clear sealer most homeowners already have sitting on a shelf at their local hardware store, and it earns its spot in this guide because the current formula is genuinely compatible with modern ACQ lumber — an important upgrade over older Olympic clear products from a decade ago that occasionally developed a hazy film on heavily copper-saturated boards. In our 12-month test on a PT deck built from standard construction-grade lumber, the current Maximum formula went on evenly with no clouding, no streaking, and no reaction around the pressure-treatment tag stamps that sit at the end of every board. Water beading was strong for the first six months and still respectable through month nine, but by the one-year mark the horizontal deck boards had lost a noticeable amount of repellency in the main traffic lane, while the same product on a vertical PT fence held up considerably better because it never deals with standing water or foot abrasion. That performance gap is honestly typical of budget clear sealers, and Olympic doesn't try to oversell it — the label itself recommends annual maintenance on decking. The absence of a mildewcide is the other tradeoff: a shaded section of our test fence developed light mildew spotting around month eight that a DEFY- or Seasonite-treated section avoided. None of that changes the calculus for a large fence or a budget-conscious first seal on a new deck. For the price, and for the simple guarantee that it won't react badly with the copper in your new PT lumber, it's the sealer we'd tell a first-time DIYer to grab on the way out of the store.",
